    narr:narration """On 2026-08-22, QuintonFairweather announces the adoption of Zypherion for the analytics pipeline — a declarative decision settling the technology choice [adoption announcement](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_1). The justification rests on a single performance claim: Zypherion handles columnar queries 15x faster than the current setup, voiced as an expert-rational-persuasion claim rather than a measured result [15x performance claim](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_2). A migration timeline is set for the following quarter, stated as a future-tensed decision under pressure rather than a concrete plan with milestones [migration timeline](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_3). Three composite editorial restatements recap the same decision in matter-of-fact register — database choice, performance figure, and timeline — all signed by Quinton as principal and carrying informational power rather than the expert or authority footing of the original utterances [database recap](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_4), [performance recap](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_5), [timeline recap](narr:Expr_1LifecycleStepA_6). The hub's frame asks whether the justification and rollout hold up as they play out; at this point every child is co-temporal and supportive, with no challenge or post-decision evidence yet recorded.""" ;
